</div>
<div id="p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:397.5pt;height:0.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></span></p>
</div>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Homicidal Chauffeur / Car Tag</h2>

<section id="S8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.1 </span>Update Equations</h3>

<div id="S8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The problem studied in <a href="#S4" title="4 Evaluation on Car Tag ‣ Foundation Model Self-Play: Open-Ended Strategy Innovation via Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is a 2-dimensional Car Tag <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Isaacs &amp; Corporation, 1951</a>)</cite> problem where we have two agents that are navigating around the XY-plane: one evader, e, and one pursuer, p. The pursuer has a minimum turn radius of <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and moves at speed <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> according to heading-angle <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> while the evader moves at speed <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> according to heading-angle <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}&gt;s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}&gt;s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The next <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xy</annotation></semantics></math>-locations (i.e., the transition dynamics of the MDP) for each agent are defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S8.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\theta}=\frac{s_{1}}{R}\phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\theta}=\frac{s_{1}}{R}\phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S8.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{p,{t+1}}=x_{p,t}+s_{1}\sin({\phi_{t-1}+\dot{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{p,{t+1}}=x_{p,t}+s_{1}\sin({\phi_{t-1}+\dot{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S8.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{p,{t+1}}=y_{p,t}+s_{1}\cos({\phi_{t-1}+\dot{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{p,{t+1}}=y_{p,t}+s_{1}\cos({\phi_{t-1}+\dot{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S8.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{e,{t+1}}=x_{e,t}+s_{2}\sin(\psi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{e,{t+1}}=x_{e,t}+s_{2}\sin(\psi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S8.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{p,{t+1}}=y_{e,t}+s_{2}\cos(\psi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{p,{t+1}}=y_{e,t}+s_{2}\cos(\psi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S8.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi_{t+1}=\dot{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi_{t+1}=\dot{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.2 </span>Car Tag Starter Policies</h3>

<div id="S8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We supply here the starter policies for the FMSP algorithms when applied to the Car Tag domain as mentioned in <a href="#S4" title="4 Evaluation on Car Tag ‣ Foundation Model Self-Play: Open-Ended Strategy Innovation via Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="S8.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_python ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-border-color:#999999;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline">
