<section id="S8.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.5 </span>Car Tag Code Policies</h3>

<div id="S8.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below are example generated policies discussed in <a href="#S4" title="4 Evaluation on Car Tag ‣ Foundation Model Self-Play: Open-Ended Strategy Innovation via Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Policies with “phi” in the class name are pursuer policies while policies with “psi” in the class name are evader policies. All policies below were written by GPT-4o.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Monte-Carlo-Tree-Search Pursuer Policy seen in <a href="#S4.F4" title="In 4 Evaluation on Car Tag ‣ Foundation Model Self-Play: Open-Ended Strategy Innovation via Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>:</p>
